[41.510882, "o", "adrs/2026-07-05-push-time-validation-via-no-mistakes-gate.md - Route feature branch pushes through the no-mistakes validation gate\r\n  Read when: Shipping feature branches from this starter.; Re-evaluating push-time validation, PR creation, or progress-log requirements.\r\n"]
[41.511318, "o", "adrs/2026-07-27-cloudflare-workers-hosting-option.md - Adopt Cloudflare Workers with OpenNext as a second supported hosting path\r\n  Read when: Changing the `apps/web` deployment strategy.; Re-evaluating Vercel and Cloudflare hosting support.; Adding provider-specific runtime bindings or deploy commands.\r\n"]
[41.511659, "o", "adrs/2026-10-04-native-skill-layout.md - Store all skills in the harness-native .agents/skills layout with .claude/skills as a symlink\r\n"]
[41.511754, "o", "  Read when: Adding, moving, renaming, or vendoring a skill.; Re-evaluating where agent skills or workflow prompts live in this starter.\r\n"]
[41.512181, "o", "adrs/2026-10-18-release-through-pull-requests.md - Prepare package releases as pull requests and tag main only after the release merges\r\n"]
[41.512287, "o", "  Read when: Preparing, tagging, or publishing a package release.; Re-evaluating how releases interact with branch protection, CI, or the no-mistakes gate.\r\n"]
[41.51268, "o", "adrs/2026-11-18-d2-cordis-plug-in-framework.md - D2: cordis is the plug-in framework, pinned to one exact version, and only packages/core imports it\r\n"]
[41.512734, "o", "  Read when: Adding a plug-in, a port or a plug-in list.; Changing the version of cordis or a boundary test.\r\n"]
[41.513029, "o", "adrs/2026-11-18-d28-attempts.md - D28: each start of a sandbox for a task is a new attempt, and the attempt number is in the pass, each trail row and each cost row\r\n  Read when: Working on the trail, the costs, the pass or the sandbox port.; Adding a table key that a turn can write again.\r\n"]
[41.513323, "o", "adrs/2026-11-18-d3-pi-durable-loop-engine.md - D3: pi-durable is the engine of the loop, pinned to one exact version, as one plug-in behind a port\r\n"]
[41.513399, "o", "  Read when: Working on the loop of a bot or the loop of Petra.; Changing the version of pi-durable or the journal of a task.\r\n"]
[41.51362, "o", "adrs/2026-11-18-d4-two-loops.md - D4: Petra runs in one Durable Object for each account, and the loop of each bot runs in a sandbox, one for each attempt\r\n"]
[41.513699, "o", "  Read when: Deciding where a part of the platform runs.; Working on the sandbox port, the launcher or the runner.\r\n"]
[41.514001, "o", "adrs/2026-11-18-d5-hook-points-and-gateway.md - D5: the hook points of the loop are cordis events called from the pi-durable hooks, and the rules run on Cloudflare behind one gateway\r\n"]
[41.514085, "o", "  Read when: Adding or changing a hook point of the loop.; Adding or changing a call of the gateway.\r\n"]
[41.514394, "o", "adrs/2026-11-18-d6-two-writers.md - D6: only two writers write the database, Petra for the data of her account and the Platform object for the data that has no account\r\n"]
[41.514405, "o", "  Read when: Adding a write to the database.; Adding a table or changing the database port.\r\n"]
[41.514668, "o", "adrs/2026-11-18-d7-neon-with-row-level-security.md - D7: the database is one Neon Postgres database, with row-level security and three database roles as the second safety layer\r\n"]
[41.514711, "o", "  Read when: Adding a migration, a table or a database role.; Working on the isolation of accounts.\r\n"]
[41.514981, "o", "adrs/2026-11-18-d8-one-id-for-each-action.md - D8: the id of an action is the task id and the tool-call id, and the gate never does the same id two times\r\n  Read when: Working on the gate, an action tool or the journal of a task.; Changing the rules for an action that comes again.\r\n"]
[41.515234, "o", "adrs/2026-11-18-two-push-paths.md - Push through the no-mistakes gate when it is installed, and run the four checks and open a normal pull request when it is not\r\n"]
[41.515245, "o", "  Read when: Pushing a branch of a PRD 1 task.; Working in a session that has no no-mistakes gate, such as an Amp orb.\r\n"]
[41.51552, "o", "agent-skills.md - Curated vendored Vercel, Addy Osmani, Matt Pocock, and Chrome DevTools agent skills plus the policy for keeping them pinned\r\n"]
[41.515531, "o", "  Read when: Working on React, Next.js, UI review, or interaction patterns in this starter.; Working on context setup, testing strategy, review rigor, security checks, or ADRs in this starter.; Working on architecture review, refactoring, domain vocabulary, or testable module interfaces.; Diagnosing frontend or Node.js memory leaks with heap snapshots.; Adding, moving, or renaming a skill directory under `.agents/skills/`.; Updating vendored skills from `vercel-labs/agent-skills`, `addyosmani/agent-skills`, `mattpocock/skills`, or `ChromeDevTools/chrome-devtools-mcp`.; Deciding whether a new upstream skill belongs in the default starter layer.\r\n"]
